acceptance_criteria: Versioned evidence-backed disjoint partition declarations with immutable operand and declaration pins; Explicit reviewed addition preserves union population source evidence uncertainty and unknowns while incompatible contexts refuse before writes; Real no-git SDK trackers verify native CAS process concurrency crash replay backward reads and behavioral revert proofs; README and ARCHITECTURE document a pinned public tracker example and scoped limits
parent: pm-unit-release
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T21:16:56.345Z",codex-sol,"PR #4 explicitly defers reviewed compatibility/disjoint partition declarations, general product/division/exponent unit AST, weighted ratio aggregation and immutable declaration pins. PR #5 only adds cross-window comparison. Keep open; concurrent declaration work and PR #7 are outside this closure audit."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:28.234Z",codex-astra,"Scope: deliver versioned evidence-backed disjoint partition declarations, native CAS/replay, immutable operand and declaration pins, and safe exact addition. Preserve existing version-1 records. General compatibility mappings, product/division/exponent unit AST, and weighted ratio aggregation will be separate Feature items with explicit acceptance criteria. Validate with real no-git SDK trackers, shared OS-process writers, crash/replay boundaries and isolated behavioral reverts."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:29.432Z",codex-astra,"Split remaining original scope into pm-unit-compatibility, pm-unit-unit-ast and pm-unit-weighted-ratios. New declarations upgrade only their owner to state version 2; version-1 reads and exact-context derivations remain unchanged. Review attribution is submitted evidence, not authenticated approval or a proof of real-world disjointness."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:30.640Z",codex-astra,"Focused declaration suite: 10/10 passed using real SDK trackers. Independent OS callers raced at before_update: exactly one committed and the other received revision_conflict; explicit re-review preserved both declarations. SIGKILL before and after the durable update converged on one declaration and audit event using the original key. Public read-only tracker copy at 0578835e5d5b46aac334bb8368905deb04530b61 contains seven Features plus one Epic; pinned membership evidence reproduces eight items. Lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gates passed. Full coverage, packed consumers and isolated behavioral reverts are in progress."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:31.762Z",codex-astra,"The required pm test run completed successfully: 10 tests, 10 passed, zero failed/skipped/cancelled. Linked command includes build, test typecheck and the three declaration test files. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so this comment preserves the successful result without changing tracker settings. The initial full suite passed 88/88; its coverage measurement was invalidated by a concurrent rebuild and is being rerun serially before any coverage claim."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:33.102Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs: all 10 new safeguard removals failed in disposable emitted-code copies, covering admission, operand fingerprints, semantic boundaries, evidence capacity, immutable declaration fingerprints, CLI dispatch, cross-process native CAS, process-kill replay, union identity and transitive declaration witnesses. The linked-worktree SDK health check reports merge-driver configuration drift against the enclosing repository despite Git resolving this package correctly; no other repository was changed. Full gates will run in a standalone package clone to isolate that SDK discovery issue."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:34.652Z",codex-astra,"Opened PR #8 at commit de51442 with the implementation, tracker split, docs, public fixture and ten isolated behavioral revert proofs; the unchanged implementation also passed the revert verification. CodeRabbit review was queued immediately after opening, independently of CI. Full npm and Bun gates are running serially in a standalone package clone."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:36.031Z",codex-astra,"Self-review corrected the public-example acquisition metadata: re-acquired the same pinned public snapshot through a complete SDK read in a disposable copy and recorded its actual retrieval timestamp. The example now uses that timestamp for observation and review attribution instead of generic fixture dates, while preserving the same eight native identities and revisions. Production code is unchanged."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:37.186Z",codex-astra,"npm run release:check passed in the standalone clone at de51442 with isolated Git configuration: 88/88 tests, 625/625 statements, 444/444 branches, 122/122 functions, 560/560 lines across eight emitted files; production audit zero vulnerabilities; 41 allowlisted packed files; npm/Node and native Bun consumers each exercised 30 CLI commands without Git, including Node 22 and 26 SDK checks; all 50 behavioral safeguard removals failed and the unchanged implementation passed. The validation clone is now updated to c4776ed for bun run release:check, including the corrected acquisition timestamp."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:38.251Z",codex-astra,"bun run release:check passed at c4776ed: 88/88 tests, 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines at 625/444/122/560 covered counters, packed npm/Node and native Bun acceptance (30 CLI commands each, Git absent), and 50 expected behavioral revert failures followed by passing unchanged-code verification. Validated packed artifact SHA-256: 748ffb31a4f37dd918b5949c80c69e2a9a8603a2e80315ef7898e360497ba172. Implementation and local verification are complete for this disjoint-partition slice; compatibility mappings, unit AST and weighted ratios remain the three linked Feature follow-ups. PR #8 remains open. CodeQL passed on c4776ed; Node 22/26 CI jobs and the shared CodeRabbit queue are still pending, with zero completed bot review rounds so far. Final-head CI/review receipts will be maintained in the PR body. No items are closed; the orchestrator owns acceptance and merge."
  "2026-11-09T11:40:39.451Z",codex-astra,Main advanced with the exact-conversion boundary fix while review was queued. Integrating that change preserves its three conversion revert proofs alongside all ten partition proofs; the only textual conflict is the shared revert-runner selection and restoration list. The combined head will rerun focused tests and both full release gates before handoff.
  "2026-11-09T11:40:40.867Z",codex-astra,"Integrated main commit 2cb8aee without changing its tracker item or history. Combined focused validation passed 13/13 with zero skipped or cancelled: npm run build && npm run build:test && node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/partitions.test.ts test/partition-process.test.ts test/partition-public.test.ts test/conversion-boundary.test.ts. The revert runner retains all 53 safeguard removals and both focused selectors. Final combined-head full-gate, CI and manual-review receipts will be recorded in PR #8; prior green CI applies only to the earlier head. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; the item remains in progress."
  "2026-11-09T11:42:03.140Z",pi-glm,"Review round (PR #8, CodeRabbit thread on the declaration admission flow): verified the finding. An over-limit declaration (operands plus evidence merging to more than sixteen distinct source fragments) was admitted durably and only failed at derivation, after consuming a declaration slot, a replay slot and the version-2 upgrade. Fix: declaration admission now previews the authorized addition through the same exported evaluator the derive path uses, so limit_exceeded refuses before any durable side effect; no second copy of capacity or precision logic exists. A same-class self-review found the preview also catches exact-precision and interval-corner overflow at admission, which a literal sixteen-fragment guard alone would have missed."
  "2026-11-09T11:42:04.422Z",pi-glm,"Revert proof for the review fix: node test/revert.acceptance.ts --partitions-only reports 11/11 expected behavioral failures, including the new declaration-admission-preview entry whose removal fails the capacity and precision admission regressions, followed by a passing unchanged implementation. New regression tests: partition admission refuses exact operands whose reviewed sum cannot persist (sixteen-fragment and eighty-digit precision cases refuse before any write, native history unchanged), plus a post-admission over-capacity declaration refusal in the refusals suite."
  "2026-11-09T11:42:05.567Z",pi-glm,"Integrated current main (dependency bumps and closure audit) after the branch fell behind. The shared tracker item and its history were taken from main and this branch's intended records were re-recorded with the pinned CLI, so the branch history is a byte-identical prefix-extension of main's. Full suite 92/92 tests with zero skipped or cancelled; linked focused suite 11/11; typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass at the review head."
  "2026-11-09T12:57:26.051Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: branch and remote agree at a4f3d3a and current main is fully integrated. Reusing this item and PR #8. Fetched all review threads and their complete comments: one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVk5Fqc60vmtk; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Preserving the admission preview fix and existing regressions; independently reviewing the whole diff and rerunning final validation. No review thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-09T12:58:38.913Z",codex-agent,"Independent self-review confirms the preview runs on a structured clone before native CAS and replay persistence; readState validates historical declaration pins without applying the new admission preview. Added a no-git real-tracker compatibility regression reproducing the pre-preview persisted declaration and receipt: over-capacity declarations still read and replay unchanged, while derivation refuses without writes. Added a separate behavioral revert entry for the provenance-capacity regression; the existing preview revert entry covers exact precision. No additional production defect was found across the full PR diff."
  "2026-11-09T13:05:12.261Z",codex-agent,"Continuation verification: focused declaration tests pass 12/12, including the historical over-capacity read/replay compatibility regression. The linked pm test run passed 11/11 before that additional regression; source-workspace focused validation then passed all 12. Full npm coverage passes 93/93 with zero skipped/cancelled and exactly 100 percent across eight emitted production files (629 statements, 446 branches, 122 functions, 564 lines). Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 90 documented declarations, identity/privacy, authoritative tracker health, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), 41-file package allowlist, changelog and publish attestation pass. Packed npm/Node and native Bun acceptance passes 1/1 with Git absent; full behavioral revert gate is still running. All changed histories preserve main as a byte-identical prefix."
  "2026-11-09T13:07:31.488Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof for unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVk5Fqc60vmtk (production fix dfd5550d86a23735479916f9d3cba19c4358889d; original regression commit 40383ecb70df33f56b09e7053b3009850ddb4eec): npm run test:revert removed only the evaluate(state, add-expression) admission call in independent disposable emitted-code copies. The partition addition conservatively propagates intervals unknowns and evidence capacity regression failed when the provenance admission preview was removed; the partition admission refuses exact operands whose reviewed sum cannot persist regression independently failed when the same preview was removed. All 55 safeguard removals have failed behaviorally as expected, including 12 partition cases; unchanged-code verification is still running. Historical declarations remain readable and replayable without rerunning the new admission policy."
  "2026-11-09T13:07:40.825Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check completed successfully in the isolated package clone with isolated Git configuration. All 93 tests pass at unchanged 100 percent coverage thresholds; packed acceptance passes 1/1 (30 CLI commands each through npm/Node and native Bun, Git absent), and 55/55 behavioral safeguard removals fail as expected followed by passing unchanged-code verification. Captured package SHA-256: 05c37d0067e00d0919b50f712f207ffd75666dcae578ed1a7d64f9fd75032e5e. Starting bun run release:check serially against the same implementation and updated tracker records."
  "2026-11-09T13:15:03.855Z",codex-agent,"Full bun run release:check passed at faa00e1dd10763a2d6f5d449d7380b89389eeaed: 93/93 tests, zero skipped/cancelled, 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines (629/446/122/564 counters across eight emitted files), packed acceptance 1/1 with 30 CLI commands each through npm/Node and native Bun with Git absent, and 55/55 expected behavioral revert failures followed by passing unchanged implementation. Both npm and Bun full release gates completed at unchanged thresholds without timeouts or retries. Both captured the identical 41-file package SHA-256 05c37d0067e00d0919b50f712f207ffd75666dcae578ed1a7d64f9fd75032e5e. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, tracker health, identity/privacy, changelog, production audit and publication-attestation checks all pass. No new CLI/SDK defect was found; linked-test result tracking remains disabled by existing project policy, so comments preserve receipts."
  "2026-11-09T13:15:04.651Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: PR #8 has one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVk5Fqc60vmtk, valid and fixed by dfd5550 with original regression tests in 40383ec and independent capacity revert plus historical compatibility evidence in faa00e1. No Outside diff range findings were present and whole-diff self-review found no additional production defect. Prior-head CI remains queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-unit/actions/runs/42612509408 and CodeQL at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-unit/actions/runs/42612509412; these are not final-head approval. Fresh exact-head CI run URLs and status will be recorded in the existing PR body and final report after pushing the receipt commit. CodeRabbit and Sourcery checks were skipped, cubic was neutral; none is review approval. Releasing only this claim, retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification. No thread reply/resolution, merge or release."
